1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:08,466
MARY: Good night, love.
JOHN: Sweet dreams, Sam.

2
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:11,552
DEMON:
Sammy, you're my favorite.

3
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:14,639
Does this mean
I have demon blood in me?

4
00:00:15,641 --> 00:00:17,934
It's you. Ah!

5
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:22,814
Mary.

6
00:00:24,483 --> 00:00:27,068
Our whole lives,
we've been searching for this demon.

7
00:00:27,236 --> 00:00:29,696
That thing killed Jess.
That thing killed Mom.

8
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:33,241
-Sam, I'm sorry.
-For what?

9
00:00:33,409 --> 00:00:34,826
-Who are you?
-Castiel.

10
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:37,453
I gripped you tight
and raised you from perdition.

11
00:00:37,621 --> 00:00:39,706
-What are you?
CASTlEL: An angel of the Lord.

12
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:43,334
JOHN: Samuel Colt made a special gun.
This gun can kill anything.

13
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:48,756
DEAN: Why would an angel
rescue me from hell?

14
00:00:48,924 --> 00:00:52,593
Because God commanded it.
Because we have work for you.

15
00:01:34,762 --> 00:01:36,471
Ready?

16
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:38,723
Definitely.

17
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:53,321
[SCREAMlNG]

18
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:59,035
CASTlEL:
Hello, Dean.

19
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:01,996
What were you dreaming about?

20
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:07,877
What, you get your freak on
by watching other people sleep?

21
00:02:08,337 --> 00:02:11,798
-What do you want?
-Listen to me.

22
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:15,134
-You have to stop it.
-Stop what?

23
00:02:17,888 --> 00:02:19,639
COP:
Move it, buddy.

24
00:02:20,432 --> 00:02:22,600
-You can't sleep here.
-Okay.

25
00:02:22,768 --> 00:02:25,394
-Sleep where?
-Anywhere but here.

26
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,045
[BEEPlNG]

27
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:58,386
Perfect.

28
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:11,607
[THE ALLMAN BROTHERS'
"RAMBLlN' MAN" PLAYS ON JUKEBOX]

29
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:23,744
Hey, where the hell am l?

30
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:25,246
Jaybird's Diner.

31
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:30,418
Yeah. Thanks. l mean city and state.

32
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,588
Lawrence, Kansas.

33
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:37,341
-Lawrence.
-Hey, you okay, buddy?

34
00:03:38,302 --> 00:03:39,719
Yeah.

35
00:03:39,887 --> 00:03:41,262
Tough night.

36
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:46,517
-Hey, coffee here, Reg.
REG: Okay, coming right up.

37
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:50,521
Can you tell me
where l can get reception on this thing?

38
00:03:51,607 --> 00:03:53,149
The USS Enterprise?

39
00:03:56,862 --> 00:03:58,738
Thanks. Nice threads.

40
00:03:58,906 --> 00:04:00,781
You know Sonny and Cher
broke up, right?

41
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:02,116
[DEAN CHUCKLES]

42
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:04,243
Sonny and Cher broke up?

43
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:29,226
[MOUTHING]
'73.

44
00:04:29,603 --> 00:04:30,770
DODDS:
Hey, Winchester.

45
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:34,815
Son of a bitch. How you doing, corporal?

46
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:36,651
-Hey, Mr. D.
-l heard you were back.

47
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:39,362
JOHN: A little while now.
DODDS: Good to have you home.

48
00:04:39,529 --> 00:04:41,656
-Damn good.
[WHlSPERS] Dad?

49
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:44,867
-Well, say hello to your old man for me.
-You got it, Mr. D.

50
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:52,959
Do we know each other?

51
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,381
I guess not.

52
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,472
-Take it easy, pal.
-Yeah.

53
00:05:19,653 --> 00:05:21,278
[SCREAMlNG]

54
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:32,248
[CHURCH BELL RlNGING]

55
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:47,555
-What is this?
-What does it look like?

56
00:05:47,723 --> 00:05:49,181
-ls it real?
-Very.

57
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:53,436
Okay, so, what, angels got their hands
on some DeLoreans? How did l get here?

58
00:05:54,104 --> 00:05:56,272
Time is fluid, Dean.

59
00:05:56,732 --> 00:05:58,899
It's not easy,
but we can bend it on occasion.

60
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:01,527
Bend it back.
Tell me what the hell l'm doing here.

61
00:06:01,695 --> 00:06:03,404
I told you.

62
00:06:03,572 --> 00:06:04,739
You have to stop it.

63
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:07,950
Stop what? What,
is there something nasty after my dad?

64
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:10,202
[CAR HORN HONKlNG
& TIRES SCREECHlNG]

65
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:18,002
Oh, come on. What, are you allergic
to straight answers, you son of a bitch?

66
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:21,213
A fine young man like yourself
just starting out.

67
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:24,467
How about l take off another 250?

68
00:06:26,470 --> 00:06:29,138
-Let's do it.
-l'll get the paperwork.

69
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:31,724
WOMAN [ON PA]:
Lamont, you got a customer...

70
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:34,477
...in the waiting room looking
for a trade-in.

71
00:06:37,147 --> 00:06:39,106
DEAN:
That's not the one you want.

72
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:41,358
You following me?

73
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:46,030
No, no. I was just passing by. l never
got to thank you for the cup of coffee.

74
00:06:46,198 --> 00:06:48,449
-l was a little out of it.
-More than a little.

75
00:06:48,617 --> 00:06:50,493
Let me repay the favor.

76
00:06:51,495 --> 00:06:53,496
-This is the car you want.
-Oh, yeah?

77
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:55,331
You know something about cars?

78
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:57,249
Yeah.

79
00:06:57,417 --> 00:07:00,127
Yeah. My dad taught me
everything I know.

80
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:02,797
And this.... This is a great car.

81
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:12,223
Three-twenty-seven 4-barrel, 275 horses.
Little TLC, this thing is cherry.

82
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:15,810
You know, man, you're right.

83
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:18,479
Well, what are you buying that thing for?

84
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:20,356
Kind of promised someone I would.

85
00:07:20,941 --> 00:07:23,317
Over a '67 Chevy?

86
00:07:23,485 --> 00:07:25,986
I mean, come on,
this is the car of a lifetime.

87
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:28,948
Trust me, this thing's
still gonna be badass when it's 40.

88
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,204
John Winchester.

89
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:38,207
Thanks.

90
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:42,002
Dean Van Halen. And thank you.

91
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:49,176
I was in pretty rough shape
this morning, huh?

92
00:07:49,344 --> 00:07:50,928
No kidding.

93
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:53,764
I've been hung-over before,
but, hey, I was--

94
00:07:53,932 --> 00:07:56,267
I was getting chills in that diner.

95
00:07:56,434 --> 00:07:58,978
-You didn't feel any cold spots, did you?
-Nope.

96
00:08:00,981 --> 00:08:05,609
I swore l smelled something weird too,
you know? Like rotten eggs.

97
00:08:05,861 --> 00:08:07,778
You didn't smell any sulfur, by chance?

98
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:10,322
-No.
-No.

99
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:14,994
-There been any cattle mutilations rec--?
-Okay, mister, stop it.

100
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:18,747
Yeah. lf only l knew what to stop.

101
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:24,253
Listen, watch out for yourself, okay?

102
00:08:27,174 --> 00:08:28,507
Yeah, sure.

103
00:08:33,763 --> 00:08:36,974
WOMAN [ON PA]: Johnny, there's
a customer for you in the waiting room.

104
00:08:37,142 --> 00:08:39,268
-Johnny, customer in the waiting room.
-So?

105
00:08:42,189 --> 00:08:43,314
I'll take this one.

106
00:09:06,713 --> 00:09:07,755
JOHN:
Hey.

107
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:10,633
What's this?

108
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,177
-My car.
-What happened to the van?

109
00:09:13,345 --> 00:09:17,264
Mary, this is better than the van.
It's got a 327, a 4-barrel carburetor.

110
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,768
Mom.

111
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:31,654
Sammy, wherever you are...

112
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:34,281
...Mom is a babe.

113
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:36,867
I'm going to hell.

114
00:09:37,035 --> 00:09:38,327
Again.

115
00:09:38,495 --> 00:09:41,205
-l should just talk to him.
-My dad's being my dad, John.

116
00:09:41,373 --> 00:09:43,207
-lt's not you.
-How's it not me?

117
00:09:43,375 --> 00:09:47,253
-He's been like this for how many years?
-He's protective over me, that's all.

118
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,545
He doesn't want me to--

119
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:51,465
Hook up with a mechanic
from a family of mechanics?

120
00:09:51,633 --> 00:09:52,883
No.

121
00:09:53,677 --> 00:09:55,427
Hey...

122
00:09:56,096 --> 00:10:00,474
...l love you for exactly what you are.

123
00:10:01,059 --> 00:10:02,142
I'll be right back.

124
00:10:17,701 --> 00:10:19,034
Why are you following us?

125
00:10:23,123 --> 00:10:24,623
DEAN:
Are you crazy?

126
00:10:28,712 --> 00:10:32,506
-You've been trailing us since my house.
-l don't know what you're talking about.

127
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:38,053
Okay, how about we talk about this, huh?

128
00:10:38,221 --> 00:10:40,097
Let me go.

129
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:49,064
Are you a hunter?

130
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:11,337
-See you later?
-lf you're lucky.

131
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:32,358
MARY:
Dean, right?

132
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:38,530
-l'm not sure you should come in.
-You can trust me.

133
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:42,868
I mean, come on, we're all hunters, right?
I mean, we're practically family.

134
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:48,082
-Yeah, thing is, my dad, he's a little--
-Oh, I gotta meet him.

135
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:49,458
You've heard of him?

136
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,628
Clearly not enough.

137
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:56,382
So you're a hunter?
Well, tell me something, Mr. Hunter.

138
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:58,884
You kill vampires with wooden stakes
or silver?

139
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:01,303
Neither. You cut their heads off.

140
00:12:02,889 --> 00:12:05,974
-So did I pass your test?
-Yep.

141
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:09,061
-Now get out of my house.
-Dad.

142
00:12:09,229 --> 00:12:12,064
I don't trust other hunters.
Don't want their help.

143
00:12:12,232 --> 00:12:15,150
-Don't want them around my family.
DEANNA: Knock it off, Samuel.

144
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:16,360
He's a hunter.

145
00:12:16,528 --> 00:12:20,364
Who passed your little pop quiz, and now
I'm inviting him to dinner. You hungry?

146
00:12:20,532 --> 00:12:22,157
-Starving.
-Good.

147
00:12:22,325 --> 00:12:24,868
I'm Deanna.
You've met my husband, Samuel.

148
00:12:25,036 --> 00:12:26,912
Now wash up.

149
00:12:27,789 --> 00:12:30,666
Samuel and Deanna?

150
00:12:30,834 --> 00:12:32,292
Really?

151
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:36,213
-First time in Lawrence, Dean?
-Well, it's been a while.

152
00:12:36,381 --> 00:12:38,215
DEANNA: Yeah?
-Things sure have changed.

153
00:12:38,383 --> 00:12:40,050
I think.

154
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:43,429
You're working a job?

155
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,849
-Yeah, maybe.
-What's that mean?

156
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:49,935
It means l don't trust other hunters
either, Samuel.

157
00:12:54,441 --> 00:12:59,069
Hey, so why were you following me
and John?

158
00:12:59,237 --> 00:13:02,364
I thought something
was after your boyfriend.

159
00:13:02,532 --> 00:13:05,492
But l don't think that anymore.

160
00:13:05,702 --> 00:13:09,037
John Winchester mixing it up
with spirits? Can you imagine?

161
00:13:10,582 --> 00:13:12,207
I saw that.

162
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:16,044
-What?
-That sour-lemon look.

163
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:19,548
Hold on. John's a really, really nice...

164
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,134
...naive civilian.

165
00:13:22,886 --> 00:13:25,804
So what?
You'd rather me be with a guy like this?

166
00:13:25,972 --> 00:13:29,016
-What? No, no. No.
-Mary, of course not. lt's just that--

167
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:33,312
That's enough. Both of you.
We have company.

168
00:13:35,106 --> 00:13:37,691
So, what about you, Sam?
You working a job?

169
00:13:37,859 --> 00:13:38,942
Might be.

170
00:13:40,028 --> 00:13:42,029
He's working a job on the Whitshire farm.

171
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:46,700
-Why does that name sound familiar?
SAMUEL: lt's been all over the papers.

172
00:13:46,868 --> 00:13:49,995
Tom Whitshire. Got tangled up
in a combine a few towns over.

173
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:52,498
-That kind of thing happens.
-Why was he on it...

174
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,917
...when his crops are all dead?

175
00:13:55,585 --> 00:13:57,753
-Demonic omens?
-That's what I gotta find out.

176
00:13:58,338 --> 00:14:01,340
What about the rest of town?
Did you find anything on the web?

177
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:05,928
Of information that you have assembled.

178
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,596
Electrical storms, maybe.

179
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:11,308
The weather-service graphs
should be here on Friday.

180
00:14:11,476 --> 00:14:12,809
-By mail?
-No.

181
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:15,270
We hired a jetliner
to fly them to us overnight.

182
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:17,856
[CHUCKLES]

183
00:14:18,024 --> 00:14:21,318
You know, it sounds to me
like we might be hunting the same thing.

184
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:24,154
If we go in numbers,
we'll take care of this real quick.

185
00:14:24,322 --> 00:14:27,115
What part of "we work alone"
do you not understand, son?

186
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:39,503
-And I'm here because...?
-Family business, Mary. Family.

187
00:14:44,634 --> 00:14:48,303
What, you'd rather be waving pom-poms
at a bunch of dumb jocks?

188
00:14:54,811 --> 00:14:57,187
-Where you going?
-To do the job, Dad.

189
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:11,868
Father.

190
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:15,956
-l see you beat me here.
-The Lord is funny that way.

191
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:19,293
Beth Whitshire, this is my associate...

192
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:24,381
...our senior, senior priest, Father Cheney.

193
00:15:24,549 --> 00:15:27,968
Please accept our deepest condolences
on behalf of the county diocese.

194
00:15:28,136 --> 00:15:29,177
Thank you.

195
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:32,097
Miss Whitshire was just telling me
all about Tom...

196
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:35,809
...and how normal and ordinary
things were on the day before his death.

197
00:15:35,977 --> 00:15:37,227
I see.

198
00:15:37,395 --> 00:15:39,563
So you didn't notice
anything unusual, ma'am?

199
00:15:39,731 --> 00:15:42,983
You mean like my husband's guts
fertilizing the back forty?

200
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:47,988
Excuse me.

201
00:16:00,877 --> 00:16:04,796
Charlie, would you like to tell
the Father here what you just told me?

202
00:16:07,050 --> 00:16:09,509
Dad drank sometimes.

203
00:16:10,595 --> 00:16:13,930
-Sometimes he got rough with Mom.
-And that's when the stranger came?

204
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:17,517
I just thought
he was some Bible-thumper, like you all.

205
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:19,478
He showed up about a week ago.

206
00:16:19,646 --> 00:16:22,522
-Saying what?
-Did l want the beatings to stop?

207
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:25,233
I just thought he was crazy.
I didn't think....

208
00:16:26,069 --> 00:16:27,903
And the next thing l know, Dad's dead.

209
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:32,783
-Am I going to jail?
-You didn't do this, Charlie.

210
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:35,202
Did the stranger want something
in return?

211
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:38,705
-He didn't want anything.
-He wasn't just handing out freebies.

212
00:16:38,915 --> 00:16:42,209
He did say something
about coming to call in 1 0 years from now.

213
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:45,253
-Maybe he'd want something then.
-Something like what?

214
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:47,339
I don't know, okay?

215
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,424
Look, l told you he was nuts.

216
00:16:55,932 --> 00:16:56,973
What do you think?

217
00:16:57,141 --> 00:17:00,727
I think he just pimped his soul
to a demon, and he doesn't even know it.

218
00:17:05,191 --> 00:17:07,818
Charlie, do you remember
what the stranger looked like?

219
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,486
Yeah.

220
00:17:10,071 --> 00:17:13,699
He was about 5'1 0". White.

221
00:17:14,492 --> 00:17:17,452
-He was kind of normal-looking, really.
-Anything else?

222
00:17:17,954 --> 00:17:20,080
-There was one thing.
-What?

223
00:17:20,248 --> 00:17:23,709
It's just,
the light hit his eyes in a weird way...

224
00:17:24,544 --> 00:17:26,378
...and for a moment, l could've sworn--

225
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:28,797
What, that they were black?
Or red, maybe?

226
00:17:28,965 --> 00:17:30,674
No.

227
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:32,634
They were yellow.

228
00:17:34,679 --> 00:17:35,721
Pale yellow.

229
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:46,565
-Slow down and talk this thing through.
DEAN: There's nothing to talk about.

230
00:17:46,733 --> 00:17:50,360
You say it was a demon. None of us
has heard of a demon with yellow eyes.

231
00:17:50,528 --> 00:17:52,070
Yeah, well, l have.

232
00:17:52,238 --> 00:17:54,531
-This thing killed my family.
-Just calm down.

233
00:17:54,699 --> 00:17:56,908
You don't get it, do you?
We're all in danger.

234
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,077
You need to get yourself someplace safe.

235
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:01,246
Not until we know
what we're dealing with.

236
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:04,166
It could be a demon, Shapeshifter,
any number of things.

237
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:06,501
I know what this thing is.

238
00:18:06,669 --> 00:18:07,669
And l'm gonna kill it.

239
00:18:07,837 --> 00:18:10,756
-That's all the talking l need to do.
-You're gonna kill a demon? How?

240
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:14,593
There's a hunter named Daniel Elkins.
Lives in Colorado. He has Colt's gun.

241
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:18,388
-The Colt.
-Yeah. I heard about the Colt.

242
00:18:18,556 --> 00:18:20,599
Used to tell it to Mary as a bedtime story.

243
00:18:20,767 --> 00:18:21,808
Well, it's real.

244
00:18:25,146 --> 00:18:28,356
All right, say that it is.
You got some kind of a crystal ball...

245
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:30,734
...telling you
where this demon's gonna be?

246
00:18:30,902 --> 00:18:33,028
Yeah, maybe I do.

247
00:18:39,076 --> 00:18:40,952
-What's this?
-lt's a list.

248
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,163
-Of what?
-My dad wrote down anyone...

249
00:18:43,331 --> 00:18:47,501
...he thought came in contact with the
yellow-eyed demon. Who, where, when.

250
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:49,920
-Why?
-Because the more he could learn...

251
00:18:50,087 --> 00:18:52,839
...the more he could figure out
why he killed my mom.

252
00:18:56,427 --> 00:18:57,552
Look.

253
00:18:58,888 --> 00:19:01,556
Whitshire farm.
I told you that name sounded familiar.

254
00:19:01,724 --> 00:19:05,811
Whitshire farm? That was two days ago.
How the hell is that on your dad's list?

255
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:11,483
My dad could see the future.

256
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:16,196
Look. He's gonna hit here
tomorrow night.

257
00:19:16,364 --> 00:19:19,407
SAMUEL: Liddy Walsh?
-Haleyville. That's close.

258
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:21,618
Well, yeah, it's about three miles, but....

259
00:19:28,376 --> 00:19:31,878
-l know you guys think l'm crazy.
-You seem like a really nice kid, Dean.

260
00:19:32,088 --> 00:19:35,048
-But, yeah, you're crazy.
-Yeah, maybe.

261
00:19:35,216 --> 00:19:38,927
But l know where this bastard's
gonna be, and l'm gonna stop it.

262
00:19:39,095 --> 00:19:41,096
Once and for all.

263
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:46,226
["GET UP AND DANCE"
PLAYS ON STEREO]

264
00:19:53,025 --> 00:19:55,861
Ahem. l'm shoving off.

265
00:19:56,487 --> 00:20:01,116
-l just wanted to say bye.
-Really? So soon?

266
00:20:01,284 --> 00:20:03,118
Yeah, well, job to do.

267
00:20:03,995 --> 00:20:06,538
Hey, I wanted to tell you...

268
00:20:06,706 --> 00:20:08,623
...you know, for what it's worth...

269
00:20:10,668 --> 00:20:13,879
...doesn't matter what your dad thinks,
I like that John kid.

270
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:17,257
-You do?
-Yeah.

271
00:20:17,508 --> 00:20:19,885
Yeah, l think you two are meant to be.

272
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:22,220
Hell, I'm depending on it.

273
00:20:22,388 --> 00:20:24,347
-What?
-Nothing.

274
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:28,518
Can l ask you a question?

275
00:20:28,686 --> 00:20:31,146
What's he like? John.

276
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:33,273
Why do you ask?

277
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,483
Just curious.

278
00:20:37,528 --> 00:20:39,404
I don't know.

279
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,407
He's sweet.

280
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:44,659
Kind.

281
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:48,246
Even after the war, after everything...

282
00:20:48,414 --> 00:20:51,750
...he still believes in happily-ever-after,
you know?

283
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:55,211
He's everything a hunter isn't.

284
00:20:58,049 --> 00:20:59,507
No offense.

285
00:21:00,051 --> 00:21:01,676
No. None taken.

286
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:05,680
Can l tell you something?

287
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:12,187
He's gonna ask me to marry him.
Tomorrow, l think.

288
00:21:12,355 --> 00:21:16,358
-Yeah?
-Dad's gonna explode.

289
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:22,530
But l don't care.
I'll run away if I have to. I just....

290
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:26,368
I love John, and....

291
00:21:29,038 --> 00:21:30,080
And what?

292
00:21:32,792 --> 00:21:34,626
I wanna get out.

293
00:21:35,711 --> 00:21:39,422
This job, this life...

294
00:21:40,341 --> 00:21:41,883
...l hate it.

295
00:21:46,138 --> 00:21:48,556
I want a family.

296
00:21:49,809 --> 00:21:51,851
I wanna be safe.

297
00:21:56,065 --> 00:22:00,652
You know, the worst thing
I can think of, the very worst thing...

298
00:22:01,112 --> 00:22:04,280
...is for my children to be raised into this
like l was.

299
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:08,493
Well, l won't let it happen.

300
00:22:11,622 --> 00:22:13,248
Yeah.

301
00:22:14,917 --> 00:22:16,626
MARY:
Hey.

302
00:22:17,378 --> 00:22:18,753
You okay?

303
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:21,548
Yeah. No, l'm fine.

304
00:22:23,843 --> 00:22:26,636
Hey, Mary...

305
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:29,305
...can I tell you something?

306
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:30,932
Sure.

307
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:33,768
Even if this sounds really weird...

308
00:22:34,270 --> 00:22:36,438
...will you promise me
that you will remember?

309
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:38,565
Okay.

310
00:22:44,113 --> 00:22:46,948
On November 2nd, 1 983...

311
00:22:50,661 --> 00:22:52,203
...don't get out of bed.

312
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:56,666
No matter what you hear,
or what you see...

313
00:23:00,212 --> 00:23:02,714
...promise me you won't get out of bed.

314
00:23:07,303 --> 00:23:08,303
Okay.

315
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:35,080
[GASPS]

316
00:23:39,001 --> 00:23:41,044
So, what, God's my copilot, is that it?

317
00:23:45,716 --> 00:23:48,093
Well, you're a regular Chatty Cathy.

318
00:23:48,761 --> 00:23:50,428
Tell me something.

319
00:23:50,596 --> 00:23:53,973
Sam would've wanted in on this.
Why not bring him back?

320
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:56,643
You had to do this alone, Dean.

321
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:02,524
And you don't care that he's tearing up
the future looking for me right now?

322
00:24:03,275 --> 00:24:05,401
Sam's not looking for you.

323
00:24:08,114 --> 00:24:12,325
All right, if I do this,
then the family curse breaks, right?

324
00:24:12,493 --> 00:24:15,036
Mom and Dad live happily ever after...

325
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:18,748
...and Sam and I grow up
playing Little League and chasing tail?

326
00:24:19,458 --> 00:24:22,710
You realize, if you do alter the future...

327
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:26,339
...your father, you, Sam,
you'll never become hunters...

328
00:24:26,507 --> 00:24:29,759
...and all those people you saved,
they'll die.

329
00:24:32,888 --> 00:24:34,222
I realize.

330
00:24:34,390 --> 00:24:37,392
-And you don't care?
-Oh, I care.

331
00:24:37,893 --> 00:24:39,727
I care a lot.

332
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:47,318
But these are my parents.
I'm not gonna let them die again.

333
00:24:47,486 --> 00:24:49,279
I can't.

334
00:24:50,489 --> 00:24:52,824
Not if l can stop it.

335
00:25:15,973 --> 00:25:17,599
[SHOTGUN COCKS]

336
00:25:17,766 --> 00:25:19,601
DANlEL:
Hold it right there, friend.

337
00:25:19,768 --> 00:25:22,103
Drop the gun. Be on your way.

338
00:25:31,113 --> 00:25:32,614
Can't do it, Daniel.

339
00:25:33,407 --> 00:25:34,490
Who the hell are you?

340
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:37,702
-A hunter, just like yourself.
-Thief's more like it.

341
00:25:37,912 --> 00:25:40,121
-l just need it for a few days.
-Not happening.

342
00:25:40,289 --> 00:25:43,499
Look, l have a chance
to save my family's lives.

343
00:25:43,667 --> 00:25:46,794
My family. But l need this gun to do it.

344
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:50,173
So if you wanna stop me, kill me.

345
00:26:15,366 --> 00:26:18,993
There are some hunters in Lawrence,
the Campbells.

346
00:26:19,161 --> 00:26:22,664
-Never heard of them.
-That's where she'll be.

347
00:26:30,506 --> 00:26:33,675
-Dean say where he was going?
-Said he was gonna kill a demon.

348
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:38,513
-Kill a demon? That's impossible.
-Yep.

349
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:41,557
-Where?
-l don't know, over in Haleyville.

350
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:43,059
The Walsh's, maybe.

351
00:26:44,561 --> 00:26:48,398
-Oh, wait. Not Liddy Walsh?
-Well, yeah, l think so.

352
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:51,901
Dad, she's a friend of mine.
We gotta help her.

353
00:26:52,069 --> 00:26:54,279
-What's wrong?
-l'll be in the car.

354
00:26:54,488 --> 00:26:55,530
Hey.

355
00:26:56,699 --> 00:26:58,700
She wants to hunt,
she doesn't wanna hunt.

356
00:26:58,867 --> 00:27:01,411
Is this some female, time-of-month thing?

357
00:27:02,288 --> 00:27:03,871
What?

358
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:06,416
I'm sorry, Liddy.

359
00:27:07,042 --> 00:27:08,543
It's metastasized.

360
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:11,045
-Where?
-His liver, his lungs.

361
00:27:11,213 --> 00:27:15,383
-lt's time we talked about arrangements.
-You have to do something. Dr. Brown.

362
00:27:15,551 --> 00:27:19,887
There is one way. A cure, actually.
But l'll need your help.

363
00:27:20,055 --> 00:27:21,889
-What do I have to do?
-Nothing.

364
00:27:22,057 --> 00:27:24,392
Just, in 1 0 years,
I'm going to come to you...

365
00:27:24,560 --> 00:27:26,269
...and ask for something then.

366
00:27:27,104 --> 00:27:29,439
-What?
-Nothing you'll miss.

367
00:27:38,866 --> 00:27:40,408
LlDDY:
Ah!

368
00:27:45,331 --> 00:27:47,582
LlDDY: Oh, my God.
-Hold that thought.

369
00:27:54,298 --> 00:27:56,591
You son of a bitch.

370
00:27:58,427 --> 00:27:59,677
DEMON:
Hello there.

371
00:28:01,430 --> 00:28:03,598
Where the hell
have they been hiding you?

372
00:28:10,105 --> 00:28:12,607
I like you. You've got a lot of spunk.

373
00:28:16,362 --> 00:28:18,112
SAMUEL:
Mary. Mary!

374
00:28:21,450 --> 00:28:24,619
-Let her go!
-Where'd you get that gun?

375
00:28:30,167 --> 00:28:32,877
Ah!

376
00:28:39,343 --> 00:28:40,385
Damn.

377
00:28:40,594 --> 00:28:44,472
-Mary, what else did he say to you?
-l told you. Just that he liked me.

378
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:49,102
What did he mean by that?

379
00:28:51,105 --> 00:28:53,189
Liddy's a strong kid. She'll be fine.

380
00:28:53,357 --> 00:28:55,983
-Are you okay?
-No, Dad, l'm pretty far from okay.

381
00:28:56,151 --> 00:28:57,735
Can we go?

382
00:29:00,239 --> 00:29:02,907
-Nice job in there.
-l missed the shot.

383
00:29:03,659 --> 00:29:05,660
Take the compliment, son.

384
00:29:05,828 --> 00:29:08,496
I'm saying that l was wrong about you.

385
00:29:12,167 --> 00:29:14,127
We need to talk alone.

386
00:29:20,342 --> 00:29:23,344
DEAN: We have to kill this thing now,
or Mary dies.

387
00:29:23,512 --> 00:29:25,555
-How do you know that?
-l just do, okay?

388
00:29:25,722 --> 00:29:28,516
-When?
-Maybe today. Probably years from now.

389
00:29:28,684 --> 00:29:29,767
But it's happening.

390
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:32,562
So, what are you,
some kind of a psychic now too?

391
00:29:35,274 --> 00:29:36,858
No.

392
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:40,027
All right, listen to me.

393
00:29:42,448 --> 00:29:44,449
Now, this is gonna sound a little--

394
00:29:45,868 --> 00:29:48,411
Actually, it's gonna sound
massively, massively crazy.

395
00:29:48,579 --> 00:29:50,371
Okay.

396
00:29:50,747 --> 00:29:52,748
-Mary is my mother.
-Excuse me?

397
00:29:52,916 --> 00:29:54,167
And l am your grandson.

398
00:29:55,043 --> 00:29:58,171
-l know what l'm talking about.
-You wanna run that by me again?

399
00:29:58,338 --> 00:30:00,089
My real name is Dean Winchester.

400
00:30:00,257 --> 00:30:04,051
I was born January 24th, 1 979.

401
00:30:04,219 --> 00:30:07,472
My parents
are Mary and John Winchester.

402
00:30:07,681 --> 00:30:09,182
I don't have to listen to this.

403
00:30:09,349 --> 00:30:12,477
Mary gets killed
by a yellow-eyed demon in 1 983.

404
00:30:12,686 --> 00:30:15,062
And l think that this,
what happened tonight...

405
00:30:15,230 --> 00:30:17,607
...is the moment
that he caught her scent.

406
00:30:17,774 --> 00:30:21,986
Now if we don't catch this thing now
and kill it, and it gets away...

407
00:30:22,196 --> 00:30:24,405
...then Mary dies.

408
00:30:25,199 --> 00:30:29,118
So l'm asking you, please....

409
00:30:33,749 --> 00:30:36,751
Hey. You okay?

410
00:30:36,919 --> 00:30:39,712
You promised you'd take me away.

411
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:41,714
Of course I did.

412
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:45,343
Do it now.

413
00:30:53,644 --> 00:30:56,771
How did I know about the Colt?
How did I know about the demon...

414
00:30:56,939 --> 00:31:00,024
...or where it would be?
I'm not making this up, Samuel.

415
00:31:00,234 --> 00:31:03,486
Every bone in my body
is aching to put you six feet under.

416
00:31:04,738 --> 00:31:07,114
But there's something about you.
I can't shake it.

417
00:31:08,492 --> 00:31:11,953
Now, l may be crazier than you, son,
but I believe you.

418
00:31:13,247 --> 00:31:16,832
-Thank you.
-All right, how do we find this bastard?

419
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:19,669
-Right here, the list.
-And with the Colt?

420
00:31:23,674 --> 00:31:24,757
Yeah.

421
00:31:30,764 --> 00:31:32,682
Okay, let me see it.

422
00:31:37,854 --> 00:31:40,523
Sorry, l don't let anybody hold it.

423
00:31:40,691 --> 00:31:42,024
I'm your grandfather.

424
00:31:43,485 --> 00:31:46,070
-Nothing personal.
-Sure, it is.

425
00:31:46,530 --> 00:31:49,490
Especially when
it's me you're trying to kill.

426
00:32:11,013 --> 00:32:13,180
Future boy, huh?

427
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:21,856
I only know one thing that's got
the juice to swing something like that.

428
00:32:22,024 --> 00:32:24,817
You must have friends in high places.

429
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:27,320
So l kill your mommy?

430
00:32:28,322 --> 00:32:32,033
That's why you came all this way
to see little old me?

431
00:32:32,534 --> 00:32:34,160
Oh, l came here to kill you.

432
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:36,537
Hey.

433
00:32:37,539 --> 00:32:39,457
Wait a minute.

434
00:32:40,709 --> 00:32:43,044
If that slut Mary is your mommy,
are you...?

435
00:32:45,631 --> 00:32:47,715
Are you one of my psychic kids?

436
00:32:52,429 --> 00:32:55,640
No. Not you.

437
00:32:55,807 --> 00:32:57,183
Maybe you've got a sis.

438
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:02,730
Or a bro. That's terrific.

439
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:05,358
Means it all worked out.

440
00:33:05,567 --> 00:33:07,652
After all, that's why I'm here.

441
00:33:07,819 --> 00:33:11,697
So that's what this is about.
These deals you're making.

442
00:33:11,865 --> 00:33:15,576
-You don't want these people's souls.
-No.

443
00:33:16,620 --> 00:33:18,120
I just want their children.

444
00:33:18,705 --> 00:33:22,083
I'm here to choose the perfect parents,
like your mommy.

445
00:33:22,250 --> 00:33:23,918
Why her?

446
00:33:24,086 --> 00:33:26,921
-Why any of them?
-Because they're strong.

447
00:33:27,089 --> 00:33:29,507
They're pure. They eat their Wheaties.

448
00:33:29,675 --> 00:33:32,802
My own little master race.
They're ideal breeders.

449
00:33:34,304 --> 00:33:37,723
Oh, get your mind out of the gutter.
No one's breeding with me.

450
00:33:37,891 --> 00:33:39,809
Though Mary....

451
00:33:40,977 --> 00:33:45,731
Man, l'd like to make an exception.
So far, she's my favorite.

452
00:33:46,316 --> 00:33:47,650
[GRUNTlNG]

453
00:33:51,196 --> 00:33:52,655
So why make the deals?

454
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:56,409
I need permission.
I need to be invited into their houses.

455
00:33:56,618 --> 00:33:58,911
I know, I know.
The red tape will drive you nuts.

456
00:33:59,121 --> 00:34:00,329
But in 1 0 short years...

457
00:34:00,831 --> 00:34:05,209
...it'll all be worth it. Because you know
what I'm gonna do to your sibling?

458
00:34:05,377 --> 00:34:09,296
I'm gonna stand over their crib,
and l'm gonna bleed into their mouth.

459
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:12,383
Demon blood is better
than Ovaltine, vitamins, minerals.

460
00:34:12,551 --> 00:34:16,345
-lt makes you big and strong.
-For what?

461
00:34:16,513 --> 00:34:19,724
So they can lead
your discount demon army?

462
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:23,185
-ls that your big plan?
-Please.

463
00:34:24,146 --> 00:34:27,565
My endgame's a hell of a lot bigger
than that, kid.

464
00:34:27,733 --> 00:34:30,276
Endgame? What endgame?

465
00:34:30,444 --> 00:34:32,653
Like l'm gonna tell you.

466
00:34:34,448 --> 00:34:37,199
Or those angels sitting on your shoulder.

467
00:34:37,576 --> 00:34:39,160
No.

468
00:34:39,578 --> 00:34:41,579
I'm gonna cover my tracks good.

469
00:34:41,747 --> 00:34:44,915
You can cover
whatever the hell you want.

470
00:34:45,333 --> 00:34:48,461
-l'm still gonna kill you.
-Right.

471
00:34:48,712 --> 00:34:50,337
Now, that l'd like to see.

472
00:34:50,964 --> 00:34:53,048
Maybe not today.

473
00:34:53,759 --> 00:34:58,012
But you look into my eyes,
you son of a bitch...

474
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:00,389
...because I'm the one that kills you.

475
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:06,687
[LAUGHlNG]

476
00:35:06,855 --> 00:35:09,940
SAMUEL: So you're gonna save
everybody, is that right? ls that it?

477
00:35:11,485 --> 00:35:15,696
Well, l'll tell you one person
that you're not gonna save.

478
00:35:15,864 --> 00:35:17,031
Your grandpappy.

479
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:21,702
No.

480
00:35:21,870 --> 00:35:23,454
No!

481
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:28,209
Ah!

482
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,906
Mary. Mary!

483
00:36:02,410 --> 00:36:05,663
JOHN: I guess it's no secret
why l brought you way out here.

484
00:36:06,540 --> 00:36:09,250
-John--
-l just....

485
00:36:09,417 --> 00:36:13,671
-Just let me get through this, okay?
-Okay, wait.

486
00:36:14,840 --> 00:36:17,049
There's things
you don't know about me, John.

487
00:36:17,259 --> 00:36:19,134
So?

488
00:36:22,472 --> 00:36:26,934
I will always love you
for exactly who you are.

489
00:36:31,439 --> 00:36:33,274
[POUNDING]

490
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:35,442
-What did l tell you?
-Dad.

491
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:38,070
-Sir, just listen.
SAMUEL: Now, come on.

492
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:39,822
-Dad.
SAMUEL: Stay away from her.

493
00:36:39,990 --> 00:36:41,073
You're hurting me.

494
00:36:41,283 --> 00:36:43,450
Hey, take it easy!

495
00:36:43,618 --> 00:36:45,286
MARY:
No.

496
00:36:53,712 --> 00:36:55,129
You killed him.

497
00:36:56,548 --> 00:36:58,382
Oh, not just John, sweetie pie.

498
00:37:00,844 --> 00:37:03,095
Mommy and Daddy too.

499
00:37:05,223 --> 00:37:06,307
They're all dead.

500
00:37:07,559 --> 00:37:10,060
-No.
-Yep. Afraid so.

501
00:37:10,228 --> 00:37:13,439
-You're little orphan Mary now.
-You son of a bitch.

502
00:37:13,607 --> 00:37:16,025
Sticks and stones
may break my bones.

503
00:37:18,153 --> 00:37:20,571
And they won't bring
your family back either.

504
00:37:20,739 --> 00:37:25,326
I'll kill you. l swear to God.

505
00:37:25,493 --> 00:37:28,162
Oh, let's not get nasty.

506
00:37:29,873 --> 00:37:33,459
Now, look, we've both said some things
that we regret.

507
00:37:33,627 --> 00:37:35,169
Let's...

508
00:37:37,547 --> 00:37:39,840
...kiss and make up.

509
00:37:40,842 --> 00:37:42,259
I'll tell you what.

510
00:37:42,427 --> 00:37:47,097
I'll arrange to have lover boy here
brought back breathing.

511
00:37:49,559 --> 00:37:53,020
-My parents too.
-Nope.

512
00:37:53,188 --> 00:37:55,105
Sorry, doll, it's not on the table.

513
00:37:55,857 --> 00:37:57,358
Think about it.

514
00:37:57,525 --> 00:37:59,568
You could be done with hunting forever.

515
00:37:59,736 --> 00:38:05,407
The white picket fence, station wagon,
couple of kids.

516
00:38:05,867 --> 00:38:10,537
No more monsters or fear.
I'll make sure of it.

517
00:38:10,705 --> 00:38:14,875
-What, and all it costs is my soul?
-Oh, no, you can keep your soul.

518
00:38:15,043 --> 00:38:16,585
I just need permission.

519
00:38:21,549 --> 00:38:23,509
For what?

520
00:38:23,885 --> 00:38:26,679
In 1 0 years, I need
to swing by your house for something.

521
00:38:26,888 --> 00:38:29,264
-For what?
-Relax.

522
00:38:31,434 --> 00:38:36,397
As long as l'm not interrupted,
nobody gets hurt.

523
00:38:36,564 --> 00:38:37,648
I promise.

524
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:50,703
Or you can spend the rest of your life
desperate and alone.

525
00:38:51,538 --> 00:38:53,122
Mary?

526
00:38:53,289 --> 00:38:55,416
It's a good deal.

527
00:38:57,043 --> 00:38:59,420
So, what do you say?

528
00:39:15,729 --> 00:39:17,563
No!

529
00:39:18,940 --> 00:39:21,025
Ah!

530
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:46,467
-Mary?
-John.

531
00:40:35,016 --> 00:40:37,351
I couldn't stop any of it.

532
00:40:39,104 --> 00:40:41,480
She still made the deal.

533
00:40:43,024 --> 00:40:45,692
She still died in the nursery, didn't she?

534
00:40:46,694 --> 00:40:48,987
Don't be too hard on yourself.

535
00:40:49,155 --> 00:40:51,448
You couldn't have stopped it.

536
00:40:55,995 --> 00:40:57,496
What?

537
00:40:58,373 --> 00:41:00,874
Destiny can't be changed, Dean.

538
00:41:03,753 --> 00:41:08,173
-All roads lead to the same destination.
-Then why'd you send me back?

539
00:41:08,341 --> 00:41:11,385
For the truth.
Now you know everything we do.

540
00:41:11,553 --> 00:41:13,720
What the hell are you talking about?

541
00:41:23,815 --> 00:41:24,857
Where's Sam?

542
00:41:25,900 --> 00:41:27,818
We know what Azazel did
to your brother.

543
00:41:27,986 --> 00:41:31,905
What we don't know is why.
What his endgame is.

544
00:41:32,073 --> 00:41:34,283
He went to great lengths
to cover that up.

545
00:41:35,535 --> 00:41:39,329
-Where's Sam?
-425 Waterman.

546
00:41:43,084 --> 00:41:46,003
Your brother is headed
down a dangerous road, Dean...

547
00:41:46,171 --> 00:41:48,338
...and we're not sure where it leads.

548
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:50,007
So stop it...

549
00:41:51,426 --> 00:41:52,718
...or we will.

550
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:39,973
[ENGLISH SDH]

